cent polling; the lone fresh survey shows Bennett up five"], "rationale": "Raters unanimously call this a Democratic flip and markets price Bennett near 90 percent, while the only recent poll gives her a five-point lead; Kean's incumbency and large cash-on-hand edge keep the call at Lean D rather than stronger.", "watch": "Fresh polling showing Kean closing within a couple of points, or a softening national environment, would move this back toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Thomas Kean Jr. (R) is running."]}, "overview": "New Jersey's seventh district sits at the political center, and first-term Republican Tom Kean Jr. is defending it in a year that clearly favors Democrats. Challenger Rebecca Bennett has kept pace with him in fundraising and drawn outside support while he has drawn almost none, and the contest has become the most expensive House race in New Jersey history. National raters are unanimous: all ten call the seat a Democratic flip, mostly Lean D. Markets are even more confident, pricing Bennett near 90 percent.\n\nEvidence for the challenger is broad but not deep. Only one recent poll exists, showing Bennett up five, and Kean holds a large cash-on-hand edge for the final stretch. Debates have highlighted Kean's alignment with Trump on Iran and tariffs and renewed questions about stock trades, while Bennett has added establishment and union endorsements. Bennett enters the final weeks favored by about six points, with meaningful uncertainty remaining.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8072, "margin": 5.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8017, "margin": 5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8142, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8286, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.794, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7844, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8491, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8475, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30",